<div class="nav-panel" id="primary-navigation" data-menu-panel data-open="false"><div class="nav-links"><a class="nav-link" href="/en/">Home</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/features">Features</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/how-it-works">How it works</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/use-cases">Use cases</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/plans">Plans</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/blog/">Blog</a></div><a class="nav-cta" href="/en/plans">Discover Rumman</a></div><div class="nav-controls"><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle data-label-light="Use light theme" data-label-dark="Use dark theme" aria-label="Use dark theme" title="Use dark theme"><span aria-hidden="true">☾</span></button><button class="menu-toggle" type="button" data-menu-toggle aria-controls="primary-navigation" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></div></nav></header><main id="conteudo"><section class="page-hero marketing-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">How to use</p><h1>A direct guide to organizing operations in Rumman.</h1><p class="hero-lead">See when to use each area, where to tap and what is recorded. Important actions remain under your confirmation.</p></div><div class="page-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/illustration-help.svg" width="240" height="180" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div></section><section class="section guide-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="guide-grid"><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">01</span><h2>Account and company</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>On first access or when business details change.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>More → My account → Company profile.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Account, workspace, profile and access preferences.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">02</span><h2>Customers</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>Before creating a quote, work order or rental.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Customers → New customer.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Name, optional tax ID, phone, address, company, notes and tags.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">03</span><h2>Catalog and kits</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>To standardize products, services and combinations sold together.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Operations → Catalog → New item.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Type, optional image, price, minimum stock and physical kit components.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">04</span><h2>From quote to payment</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>When a request must become execution and collection.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Operations → Quotes → Approve and convert.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Customer, items, order, reservation, picking, dispatch, receivable and income.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">05</span><h2>Inventory by location</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>When materials are spread across warehouses, stores, vehicles or events.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Operations → Inventory → Stock by location.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Balance by location, transfers, reservations, availability and movements.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">06</span><h2>Purchasing</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>When replenishment must include supplier, deadline and cash impact.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Operations → Purchasing → New order.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Supplier, items, forecast, receiving, average cost and payable.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">07</span><h2>Rentals</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>To reserve an item for a period and follow its return.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Operations → Rentals → New rental.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Customer, period, location, pickup or delivery, return, payment and completion.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">08</span><h2>Today in Rumman</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>At the beginning of the day and before closing work.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>Home → Today in Rumman.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>It does not invent facts: it prioritizes existing records and opens the correct module.</dd></dl></article><article class="guide-card"><span class="feature-code">09</span><h2>Data protection</h2><dl><dt>When to use</dt><dd>Before replacing a device or sharing operations with a team.</dd><dt>Where to tap</dt><dd>More → My account → Backup, team or synchronization.</dd><dt>What Rumman records</dt><dd>Encrypted .rumman file, chosen folder, workspace, roles, outbox and conflicts.</dd></dl></article></div></div></section><section class="section app-screens-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Current application screens</p><h2>Inventory by location and physical count.</h2><p class="lead">Real QA captures without personal data. The flow preserves the consolidated balance and keeps every difference auditable.</p></div><div class="screen-gallery"><figure><img src="/screenshots/estoque-por-local.png" width="1080" height="2400" loading="lazy" alt="Rumman screen showing inventory balance by warehouse and location"><figcaption>Balance by location, internal transfer and access to physical count.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/screenshots/inventario-fisico.png" width="1080" height="2400" loading="lazy" alt="Rumman screen during a physical inventory count"><figcaption>Physical count with difference and traceable adjustment.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="final-cta"><div class="wrap final-cta-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">Rumman · Guided Intelligent ERP</p><h2>Clearer management for work with less friction.</h2><p>Organize customers, cash flow, documents and everyday decisions in a guided Android experience.</p></d